@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Projects Integration
	Testing sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB where multiple projects are involved.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer3                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer3                           |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Engineering |
	| Code         | ZENOSBE             |
	| Type         | Group               |
	| Industry     | Engineering         |
	| Tier         | Premier             |
	| Max Contacts | 10                  |
	| Address Line | 456 Fake Street     |
	| Country      | United States       |
	| State        | California          |
	| City         | Los Angeles         |
	| Zip          | 90013               |
	| Region       | US                  |
	| Language     | English             |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBE"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBE"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBE"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	| ZENOSBE |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive  |
	| Zen OSB Engineering |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View ticket after requester on multiple projects is removed from project with no ticket
	Zendesk requesters removed from one project should not have tickets in other projects that they are still a part of affected.

	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	When I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBE"
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with ticket subject "Request Subject" should have the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject |
	| Status        | OPEN            |
	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | OSB Customer1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: View ticket after requester on multiple projects is removed from project with ticket
	Zendesk tickets by requesters who are part of mulitple projects and removed from a project with said ticket should be updated accordingly.

	Given I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	When I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with ticket subject "Request Subject" should have the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
 	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	When I go to the Organization requests tab
 	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
 	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log out and log into zendesk as "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject |
	| Status        | OPEN            |
	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | OSB Customer2                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: View ticket reassigned to user with a different default organization
	Zendesk tickets that are reassigned to a user with a different default organization should also be reassigned to the default organization of the new assignee.

	Given I assign a user the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I remove a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	When I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the ticket with ticket subject "Request Subject" should have the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
 	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	When I go to the Organization requests tab
 	Then I should not see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
 	When I update the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log out and log into zendesk as "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject |
	| Status        | OPEN            |
	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | OSB Customer3                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Organization  | Zen OSB Automotive                                 |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: View user tags after user removal from multiple projects
	Zendesk users that are part of mulitple OSB projects should be updated accordingly when removed from their OSB projects.

	Given I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer3@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"
